# Tracer: partial conjunction formation is not a local assumption.
# Before (same source and rejection):
# prop bounded_reciprocal(t R):
#     exist x R st {x != 0 and 1 / x > 0}
# Reading showed the terminal condition but not the conjunction's inner order.
#
# Now: still rejected. The first component is checked for formation, not
# adopted as true; the second requires x != 0, which is not yet a local premise.
# Reading keeps those two stages separate and publishes no definition or fact.
prop bounded_reciprocal(t R):
    exist x R st {x != 0 and 1 / x > 0}
#
# Boundary: separating the body clauses changes their formation-check order:
# exist x R st {x != 0, 1 / x > 0}
# That definition is well-formed, but supplies no existence witness by itself.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -strict -lang en -f examples/test_statements/negative/def_prop_stmt/compound-formation-order.lit
# Expected: exit 1, requirement/WD failure at x != 0, no session termination.
